Imoten is based on the pstack-for-codex fork by Aqua-123:

  https://github.com/Aqua-123/pstack-for-codex

That fork is a derivative of pstack by Lauren Tan, originally distributed in
the Cursor plugins repository under the MIT License:

  https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/d457567332aa6989e753ea289f30ea2bfbc80bc0/pstack

The imported source snapshot was pstack version 0.15.28 at commit
d457567332aa6989e753ea289f30ea2bfbc80bc0. The original license is preserved
in LICENSE.

Other skills derive from five more plugins in the same repository at commit
adf3218ca2f5b9971eedc07a76bef22df7701539, under the same MIT License:

- cursor-team-kit: check-compiler-errors, control-cli, control-ui, deslop,
  fix-ci, fix-merge-conflicts, get-pr-comments, loop-on-ci,
  make-pr-easy-to-review, new-branch-and-pr, pr-review-walkthrough (from
  pr-review-canvas), review-and-ship, run-smoke-tests,
  thermo-nuclear-code-quality-review, verify-this, weekly-review, and
  what-did-i-get-done.
- thermos: thermo-nuclear-review and thermos.
- advisor: advisor.
- cli-for-agent: cli-for-agents.
- agent-compatibility: check-agent-compatibility.

Their license is preserved in LICENSE-upstream-plugins. The file hashes and
per-file dispositions are in compatibility/plugins/.

Changes by the Imoten maintainers adapt and extend the workflows for OpenAI
Codex and Claude Code. This project is not an official Cursor, Anthropic, or
OpenAI project.
